	<title>The Merchant of Venice</title>
	<isbn>0743477561</isbn>
	<publication_year>1992</publication_year>
	<language_code>eng</language_code>
	<description>The Merchant of Venice is one of Shakespeare’s most popular comedies, but it remains deeply controversial. The text may seem anti-Semitic; yet repeatedly, in performance, it has revealed a contrasting nature. Shylock, though vanquished in the law-court, often triumphs in the theatre. In his intensity he can dominate the play, challenging abrasively its romantic and lyrical affirmations. What results is a bitter-sweet drama.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Though The Merchant of Venice offers some of the traditional pleasures of romantic comedy, it also exposes the operations of prejudice. Thus Shakespeare remains our contemporary.</description>
